# InsectAI hardware-db workshop feedback TODOs
**Workshop feedback suggestions**
- [ ] Need to figure out a way to put descriptions under the questions to clarify
- [ ] Section descriptions are often skipped; can make them a lot shorter and/or ask if understood (mandatory) to proceed
- [ ] DeviceID is confusing for users, but is difficult to generate automatically... 
*Specific for questions or sections*
=== Basic info ===
- [ ] Resolve ambiguity between contact person, data owner, creator, maintainer etc. 
- [ ] Device description: add explicit character limit and clarify purpose (i.e. "abstract explaining what your device is and does, should be understandable to a non-specialist audience.")
- [ ] Device description (i.e. device summary) should perhaps be placed later after the technical questions? 
- [ ] Add question on project duration and/or person/hours involved (as an estimate of the team size adn time invested). 
=== Contributors details ===
- [ ] Simplify questions about device creator, maintainer etc.
- [ ] Allow multiple names with separator (e.g. `;`)
- [ ] Move versioning question to device details
=== Device links ===
- [ ] Add language of documentation as a question?? 
- [ ] DOI field to accept multiple DOIs???
- [ ] Remove documentation upload
- [ ] Add "Additional resources" to capture non-standard repos or YouTube videos. 
=== Device details ===
- [ ] Device construction wording is confusing; "Custom designed parts (e.g., PCB, 3D print)". Add "Other"???
- [ ] Cost should be split into:
  - [ ] Unit Build Cost (Hardware only).
  - [ ] Deployment/Seasonal Costs (Consumables).
  - [ ] Ongoing Software/Compute Costs.
  - [ ] Assembly Time/Cost (Human hours).
- [ ] Device size, split into:
  - [ ] packaged dimensions for transport (L x W x H)
  - [ ] deployed dimensions (L x W x H)
- [ ] Remove colour
- [ ] Device material change to "primary material", with dropdown list & other
- [ ] Device mobility, simplify and enforce choice from dropdown.
- [ ] New Fields: Skills & Tools Required (for construction) as a filterable tag.
=== Component details === 
- [ ] Details abut the sensor should be asked before or at the same time as teh device details.
- [ ] Sensor type might need some logic to only show lens, resolution, framerate etc if "Optical/Camera" has been selected. 
- [ ] Power: rename "Main" to "Grid electricity"
- [ ] Move "Attractants" to to a dedicated section
- [ ] Connectivity: add USB to physical connectivity
- [ ] Clarify "Processing Unit" (e.g., Raspberry Pi, Jetson, Microcontroller).
- [ ] Data: change "Supported File Types" to a checklist. 
- [ ] Software: add specific field for On-device Software Version and Repository Link (distinct from hardware version).
=== Maintenance and repairs ===
- [ ] Repairability: Add a 1-5 scale with definitions/examples (e.g., "1 = Soldering required, 5 = Tool-free replacement").
- [ ] Maintenance: Add Maintenance Intervals (e.g., "Clean lens every 2 weeks").
- [ ] Firmware: Specify "Update Method" (Over The Air, Cable, SD Card).
=== Intended usage scope === 
- [ ] Taxonomy: convert to checklist with vernacular / scientific names. 
- [ ] Maybe add functional guild or other non-taxonomic grouping?
- [ ] Habitats: convert to a Dropdown/Checklist of standardized habitat types.
- [ ] Constraints: split ranges into Min and Max fields (e.g., Temp Min/Max °C).
- [ ] Environment: clarify "Operational Environment" (Aquatic/Terrestrial) and add IP Rating for weatherproofing.
- [ ] Target: add typical subject size range (Min/Max mm) as numeric fields.
=== Missing questions to add ===
- [ ] Labor Metrics: time required to build one unit and human hours for operation/maintenance.
- [ ] Mounting Systems: how the device attaches to the environment (e.g. tripod, tree mount, pole, etc).
- [ ] Charging infrastructure: Number of batteries, solar panel wattage, charging cycles.
- [ ] Software Specifics: distinct versioning for hardware vs. software; repository links for standalone software.
- [ ] Institution Type: categorization of the organization (NGO, Academic, Government, Commercial).
- [ ] Pros/Cons: A qualitative field for users to list known limitations or advantages of the device.
- [ ] Data Analysis Platform: Where the data is processed (local machine, cloud platform name).
=== Others === 
- [ ] Remove any mention of uploads of any kind, as we cannot host any files; provide field for links and some instructions on how to host them externally (e.g. GitHub, Zenodo)
- [ ] 

